/godot-build-scripts/pull/157, where we need to decide whether and how perfetto should be enabled by default on the production templates we provide.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4232262214/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4232340422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118401#issuecomment-4232340422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118401","id":4232340422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78RGPG","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-12T18:25:31Z","updated_at":"2026-04-12T18:25:31Z","body":"> Since Perfetto coverage is only a few hand picked methods (tracing coverage, not scripts), enabling it by default should be cheap. I guess you can interpret my approval as \"no concerns from me\"; i can't judge if people will actually use it.\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce I plan to also lo